# Flower Match – CIS-137 Lab 3 README

## Project Description

Flower Match is a memory matching game created using Swift and SwiftUI in Xcode. The goal of the game is to find all 12 matching pairs of flowers by flipping over two cards at a time.

The game uses the Model-View-ViewModel (MVVM) architecture to organize the code and separate the game data, game logic, and user interface.

Features

- 24 cards containing 12 matching flower pairs.
- Randomly shuffled cards each time the game restarts.
- Interactive card flipping.
- 3D rotation animation when cards are flipped.
- Matching cards stay face up.
- Nonmatching cards flip back over.
- Restart button to begin a new game.
- Victory message when all 12 pairs are matched.

MVVM Architecture

This project uses three main parts of the MVVM architecture.

### 1. Model – FlowerCard.swift

The Model stores the information for each flower card.

It includes:
- A unique ID for each card.
- The flower number.
- Whether the card is face up.
- Whether the card has been matched.

### 2. ViewModel – FlowerGameViewModel.swift

The ViewModel controls the game's logic and communicates between the Model and View.

It is responsible for:
- Creating the flower cards.
- Shuffling the cards.
- Handling card selections.
- Checking whether two cards match.
- Tracking matched pairs and moves.
- Restarting the game.

### 3. View – ContentView.swift

The View displays the game's user interface.

It includes:
- The Flower Match title.
- The flower card grid.
- Individual card designs.
- The restart button.
- The victory message.

